What Can You Build with Node.js?
1. Web Servers

Example:

const http = require('http');

const server = http.createServer((req, res) => {
    res.end('Hello World');
});

server.listen(3000);
2. REST APIs

Popular for:

Mobile backends
Web applications
SaaS products

Example:

User management APIs
E-commerce APIs
3. Real-Time Applications

Such as:

Chat applications
Multiplayer games
Live notifications

Examples include applications similar to:

WhatsApp
Discord
4. Streaming Applications

Examples:

Video streaming
Audio streaming
Live broadcasts
5. Microservices

Large applications often split functionality into small services.

Node.js is commonly used for microservice architectures.

6. Command-Line Tools

Examples:

npm
npx
create-react-app

Many popular CLI tools are built with Node.js.

Node.js Modules

Node.js provides built-in modules.

Examples:

Module	Purpose
http	Create web servers
fs	File system operations
