console.log(os.platform());
NPM (Node Package Manager)

Node.js comes with NPM, the world's largest software package registry.

NPM allows developers to install libraries easily.

Example:

npm install express

Popular packages:

Express.js
Axios
Lodash
Mongoose
Socket.IO
Node.js vs Browser JavaScript
Feature	Browser JS	Node.js
Runs in Browser	✅	❌
Runs on Server	❌	✅
Access File System	❌	✅
Access DOM	✅	❌
Create APIs	❌	✅
Database Access	❌	✅
Advantages of Node.js

✅ Fast execution

✅ Large ecosystem (NPM)

✅ JavaScript everywhere

✅ Excellent for real-time apps

✅ Scalable

✅ Lightweight

✅ Huge community support

Disadvantages of Node.js

❌ Not ideal for CPU-intensive tasks

Examples:

Video rendering
Heavy scientific calculations
Machine learning training

Because the main thread can become blocked.

❌ Callback complexity (though modern JavaScript uses Promises and async/await)

Example:

async function getUser() {
    const user = await fetchUser();
    return user;
}
